WEBVTT

00:00:01.626 --> 00:00:10.085
Masters — reference data
The tables the CRM's calculations read: routing, rates, risk weights, approval limits and service levels.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.960
Sign in as Kevin Lam — CRM Administrator
The CRM administrator maintains the masters

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:26.360
One tab per master — each row is an ordinary record
Edit, import, export and audit them like any other data

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:36.800
Masters are data: change a row and the next calculation uses it
The Builder is configuration: fields, forms, stages and workflows

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:44.920
Website Product Routing: what the client picks on the website
Each product goes to a business unit and a queue, with a first-contact target

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:48.640
Personal loans get a faster first call from today
Edit the Personal Loan rule

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:56.400
New queue name and first contact within 2 business hours
The business unit stays Lending, so the same team still gets the enquiries

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.120
Saved — no release, no restart
The next enquiry for a personal loan reads the new rule

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:18.240
Mélissa Bégué asks about a personal loan on the website
The same "Get in touch" form the website shows

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.800
Sent — the enquiry is in the CRM
Routing, scoring and the speed-to-lead clock run as it arrives

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:31.440
On the enquiry: the new queue and the 2-hour first-contact target
Read from the routing rule at the moment it arrived

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:38.520
The speed-to-lead clock now allows 2 business hours, not 4
Sophie Lagesse (Lending) is alerted as the deadline nears

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:43.680
Enquiries that arrived earlier keep the target they were given
A routing change applies from the next enquiry on

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:53.280
The KYC risk score adds up weights from the risk-factor master
Country risk + PEP + product + channel + occupation + ownership + activity

00:01:53.280 --> 00:02:00.440
A case under screening: risk score 102
South African resident, onboarded without meeting in person

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:05.200
Country risk 25 comes from the Country master
South Africa: FATF increased monitoring (grey list)

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:21.040
Countries (AML risk): a score from 0 to 40 for each country
Updated after each FATF plenary or sanctions change — black-listed countries score 40

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:33.960
Compliance decides that remote onboarding carries more risk
Onboarding channel “non face to face”: weight 10 → 15

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:38.680
The case still shows 102
A risk score is worked out when the case is saved — not every time a weight changes

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:46.720
Re-assess the case: open it and save
At the next edit or periodic review the case reads the current weights

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:54.000
Risk score 107: +5 from the new channel weight
Rating, EDD and the approver follow the score

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:00.360
Approval Matrices: who approves a loan, by amount
Up to MUR 5m Loans Manager · up to 20m Credit Committee · above that the Board

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:12.280
Each application reads its band from these limits
MUR 13m → Credit Committee: the approval goes to that committee

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:22.240
Service Request Catalogue: every request type
Business unit, service level in business hours, and whether it needs approval

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:33.240
A partial prepayment: 40 business hours, approval required
Each request copies these values and routes the approval to the business-unit head

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:39.160
Genesis PLR History: the prime lending rate over time
Loan pricing and each product's “Rate from” read the latest rate in effect

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:52.680
Real Estate Loan: “Rate from” = latest PLR 6.825% + the product margin −0.675%
Products & Services ▸ the product sheet

00:03:52.680 --> 00:04:01.360
A new PLR row reprices every variable-rate loan and product
Add one only after ALCO approves it, with its effective date — it applies from that day

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:10.840
FX Reference Rates: the daily TT board
Converts amounts to rupees and prices FX quotes — the forex desk publishes it each morning

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:18.160
Collateral Types & Haircuts: lending value and LTV alert levels
Read by every pledge and by the margin-call checks

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:25.720
Model Portfolios A–E: the target asset mix for each risk profile
Conservative A to Aggressive E — used by wealth mandates

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:32.520
For this tutorial, restore what we changed
Every change to a master is kept in the record's history

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:41.080
Non-face-to-face weight back to 10

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.680
Personal Loan routing back to Retail Loans, 4 business hours

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:50.600
And save the KYC case once more so it reads the restored weight

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:55.880
Back to 102
Weights and routing are as they were

00:04:56.147 --> 00:05:03.800
Masters — reference data
Change the data, not the system: the next calculation uses the new values.
